Select AI allows users to ask natural-language questions about business data. 
An LLM uses the AI Profile and database metadata to understand the user's intent and generate SQL. 
Oracle Database then executes the generated SQL and returns the actual result.
Select AI can be used with Oracle's security mechanisms and configured LLM providers.

                  User
                   │
                   │ Natural Language
                   ▼
              Select AI
                   │
                   ▼
              AI Profile
             /          \
            /            \
     LLM Model       DB Metadata
            \            /
             \          /
              ▼        ▼
          Understand Question
                  │
                  ▼
          Generate SQL Query
                  │
                  ▼
          Oracle Database
                  │
                  ▼
             Execute SQL
                  │
                  ▼
               Result
                  │
                  ▼
                User


Before using Select AI, we configure an AI Profile.

An AI Profile defines the configuration that Select AI uses when processing natural-language questions. 
It can specify the LLM provider, the LLM model, and the database schemas and objects that should be available for the AI interaction.
AI Profile
   │
   ├── LLM Provider
   ├── LLM Model
   └── Database Objects
        ├── MOVIES
        ├── ACTORS
        └── STREAMS

DBMS_CLOUD_AI ->  Oracle provides the DBMS_CLOUD_AI PL/SQL package for configuring Select AI and its AI Profiles.
